---
title: Pump restart procedure
lang: en
---

## Before you start

Complete the plant isolation briefing before this course. That briefing teaches the lockout tags used here.

For a routine restart, verify the isolation tag, inspect the pressure gauge, then ask the lead to release the pump.

---

## Optional pressure note

Open the pressure note if you need a reminder before the next question.

### Pressure note
as: accordion

If pressure rises during restart, pause the feed before opening the vent.

close: accordion

---

## Pressure check

### Pressure rises during restart. What should you do first?
as: choice

(x) Pause the feed
( ) Open the vent immediately

---

## Gauge check

Read this rule: if the gauge is below the marked safe band, stop the restart and call the lead.

### The gauge is below the safe band. What should you do?
as: choice

(x) Stop the restart and call the lead
( ) Continue until the gauge rises

---

## Worksheet

Outside this course, fill in the restart worksheet with the isolation tag, gauge reading and lead's name. Bring it to the next shift handoff.
